From 4e5008e32aab59ca738228fba007899c646900d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qineng-det <det@topogym.local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:00:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] cuda: reproducible assembly and contact candidate order
 (TopoGym determinism series 2/4)

Gradient / diagonal-Hessian assembly and contact candidate lists no longer
depend on the scheduler. Physics unchanged; only orders are fixed.

Atomics replaced:
- finite_element/fem_linear_subsystem.cu: gradient doublets atomic_add'ed
  into the global gradient (kinetic, reporters, dytopo effects) ->
  det::SegmentedAdder (det_scatter.h): stable radix sort of the doublet
  keys, run-length encode, one thread per (vertex, component) sums its run
  in production order; fixed vertices skipped as before.
- affine_body/abd_linear_subsystem.cu: reporter and dytopo gradients
  atomic_add'ed per body -> SegmentedAdder (12 per body); the diag_hessian
  atomic adds of reporter and dytopo 12x12 diagonal blocks ->
  SegmentedAdder (144 per body).
- collision_detection AtomicCountingLBVH::detect / query (linear_bvh broad
  phase): candidate pairs appended through an atomic counter, so their
  order (hence contact doublet / triplet order) followed the scheduler ->
  canonical_sort(): pairs sorted by (i, j) with cub radix sort after every
  detect / query.
- collision_detection/filters/easy_vertex_half_plane_trajectory_filter.cu:
  vertex / half-plane candidates appended through an atomic counter ->
  sorted canonically before use.
